    "text": "This is a lazy-greedy heuristic. It repeatedly signs up the library with the best estimated scan value per signup day, using a max-heap. A library's value only decreases as time advances and books get taken, so a stale heap entry is safe to re-evaluate on pop. When the work budget runs out, it stops re-evaluating and uses stale values. Output is always valid because the actual book lists are built at selection time. I have not compiled or run it against the judge data.\n\n```cpp\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint B, L, D;\nvector<int> S;\nstruct Lib {\n    int N, T, M;\n    vector<int> books; // sorted by score desc\n};\nvector<Lib> libs;\nvector<char> taken;\nlong long ops = 0;\nconst long long OPS_LIMIT = 300000000LL;\n\n// Estimated value per signup day if library j starts signup at day ts.\ndouble evalLib(int j, long long ts) {\n    const Lib& lb = libs[j];\n    long long avail = (long long)D - ts - lb.T;\n    if (avail <= 0) return 0.0;\n    long long cap = avail * (long long)lb.M;\n    double sum = 0;\n    long long cnt = 0;\n    for (int b : lb.books) {\n        ops++;\n        if (taken[b]) continue;\n        sum += S[b];\n        if (++cnt >= cap) break;\n    }\n    return sum / lb.T;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    cin >> B >> L >> D;\n    S.resize(B);\n    for (int i = 0; i < B; i++) cin >> S[i];\n    libs.resize(L);\n    for (int j = 0; j < L; j++) {\n        cin >> libs[j].N >> libs[j].T >> libs[j].M;\n        libs[j].books.resize(libs[j].N);\n        for (int k = 0; k < libs[j].N; k++) cin >> libs[j].books[k];\n        sort(libs[j].books.begin(), libs[j].books.end(),\n             [&](int a, int b) {\n                 if (S[a] != S[b]) return S[a] > S[b];\n                 return a < b;\n             });\n    }\n    taken.assign(B, 0);\n\n    priority_queue<pair<double, int>> pq;\n    for (int j = 0; j < L; j++) {\n        double v = evalLib(j, 0);\n        if (v > 0) pq.push({v, j});\n    }\n\n    long long t = 0;\n    vector<pair<int, vector<int>>> chosen;\n\n    while (!pq.empty()) {\n        auto top = pq.top();\n        pq.pop();\n        if (t >= D) break;\n        int j = top.second;\n        double nv = (ops < OPS_LIMIT) ? evalLib(j, t) : top.first;\n        if (nv <= 0) continue;\n        if (!pq.empty() && nv < pq.top().first) {\n            pq.push({nv, j});\n            continue;\n        }\n        // Select library j.\n        t += libs[j].T;\n        long long cap = ((long long)D - t) * (long long)libs[j].M;\n        if (cap <= 0) continue;\n        vector<int> list;\n        for (int b : libs[j].books) {\n            if ((long long)list.size() >= cap) break;\n            if (taken[b]) continue;\n            taken[b] = 1;\n            list.push_back(b);\n        }\n        if (list.empty()) continue;\n        chosen.push_back({j, std::move(list)});\n    }\n\n    string out;\n    out.reserve(1 << 20);\n    out += to_string(chosen.size());\n    out += '\\n';\n    for (auto& c : chosen) {\n        out += to_string(c.first);\n        out += ' ';\n        out += to_string(c.second.size());\n        out += '\\n';\n        for (size_t i = 0; i < c.second.size(); i++) {\n            if (i) out += ' ';\n            out += to_string(c.second[i]);\n        }\n        out += '\\n';\n    }\n    cout << out;\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
